    <h2>Actionable Strategies to Lower Your Cost Per Engagement</h2>
    <p>
      If your campaigns are yielding high CPE numbers, implement these proven performance optimizations:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>1. Prioritize Multi-Slide Carousel Formats</h3>
        <p>
          Carousels generate higher engagement rates than single images because users swipe multiple times. Structure your carousels as educational frameworks, before-and-after case studies, or step-by-step checklists.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>2. Front-Load the First 3 Seconds with a High-Stakes Hook</h3>
        <p>
          Eliminate slow video introductions. Open with a compelling visual question, bold contrarian statement, or immediate product transformation to stop scrollers in their tracks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>3. Prompt Comment Discussions with Open-Ended Questions</h3>
        <p>
          Close your captions with a specific, engaging prompt (e.g., <em>'Which of these 3 setups do you prefer? A, B, or C?'</em>). Lowering friction to comment triggers algorithm boosts that drive organic reach.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>4. Refine Audience Segmentation to Prevent Ad Fatigue</h3>
        <p>
          Broad, untargeted audiences scroll past ads, driving up CPE. Segment campaigns using custom lookalike audiences, engaged page interaction retargeting, and verified interest clusters.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Common Mistakes When Calculating or Interpreting CPE</h2>
    <p>
      Avoid these common pitfalls that distort engagement analytics:
    </p>

    <div class="callout-box warning">
      <div class="callout-title">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="inline-icon" style="display:inline-block; vertical-align:middle; color:#f59e0b; margin-right:6px;"><path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg> Critical Metric Pitfalls
      </div>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Avoid these analytical mistakes to ensure accurate reporting and sound budget allocation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Treating Passive Impressions as Engagements:</strong> Counting mere impressions as interactions skews your calculation and gives a false perception of engagement efficiency.</li>
      <li><strong>Ignoring Engagement Quality & Sentiment:</strong> A viral post receiving thousands of angry comments or bot spam may have an ultra-low CPE, but it harms brand equity. Always audit qualitative feedback.</li>
      <li><strong>Failing to Connect CPE with Downstream Sales:</strong> A campaign with a low CPE ($0.05) is unprofitable if none of those engaged users ever convert into paying customers. Track CPE alongside Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC).</li>
      <li><strong>Comparing B2C Consumer Benchmarks with B2B Enterprise Metrics:</strong> A $2.00 CPE on LinkedIn for an enterprise software product is often far more profitable than a $0.05 CPE on TikTok for a $10 novelty item. Always evaluate CPE in context with product margins.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Best Practices for Making Data-Driven Decisions with CPE</h2>
    <p>
      To maximize your marketing ROI using Cost Per Engagement data:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Audit Creator Partnerships Before Signing Contracts:</strong> Request historical engagement data from potential influencer partners to calculate their baseline CPE before agreeing to flat sponsorship fees.</li>
      <li><strong>Cut Underperforming Ad Creatives Early:</strong> When running paid social campaigns, identify ad variants with CPEs 50% above your account average within the first 48 hours and reallocate budget to top performers.</li>
      <li><strong>Use CPE to Guide Organic Content Calendars:</strong> Track the organic CPE equivalent of your weekly posts to double down on the formats, topics, and hooks your community loves most.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
